[2025-12-28 20:23:41] {"conversation_id":"d8e89bab-51f4-49a0-9db2-023140266160","generation_id":"dbd56205-c814-44ab-a76d-54020a2e7122","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/.cursor/AGENT.md","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"# Agent Instructions for Cursor Mental Models Demo\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is a **demo project** that creates a static, single-page website to display mental models for understanding Cursor IDE. The site loads data from JSON files, renders cards in a grid layout, supports title-based search, and shows detailed modals when cards are clicked.\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n- Minimal static website (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)\n- No build tools or frameworks required\n- Data-driven from `data/mental-models.json`\n- Demo-safe: Keep changes small and readable\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/\n├── index.html          # Main HTML skeleton\n├── styles.css          # Complete styling system\n├── app.js              # Data loading, rendering, search, modal logic\n├── data/\n│   └── mental-models.json  # Single source of truth for all mental model content\n└── .cursor/\n    ├── AGENT.md        # This file - agent instructions\n    ├── BUGBOT.md       # Automated bug detection rules\n    ├── commands/       # Custom command definitions\n    └── rules/          # Code quality rules\n```\n\n## Development Environment Setup\n\n- **No dependencies required** - This is a pure static site\n- Open `index.html` directly in a browser, or use a simple HTTP server:\n  ```bash\n  # Python 3\n  python -m http.server 8000\n  \n  # Node.js (if you have it)\n  npx serve\n  ```\n- Access at `http://localhost:8000`\n\n## Build and Run Commands\n\n- **No build step required** - This is a static site\n- **Run locally**: Open `index.html` in a browser or use a simple HTTP server\n- **Test**: Manually verify the site loads, search works, and modals open correctly\n\n## Coding Conventions\n\n### General Principles\n- **Keep it simple**: No frameworks, build tools, or complex dependencies\n- **Follow existing patterns**: Match the code style and structure already in place\n- **Demo-safe**: All changes should be small, readable, and maintainable\n\n### Code Style\n- Use semantic HTML5\n- Follow the existing CSS variable system (colors defined at top of `styles.css`)\n- Use modern JavaScript (ES6+) but keep it vanilla\n- Maintain consistent formatting with existing code\n\n### Data Structure\n- Mental models are stored in `data/mental-models.json` as a JSON array\n- Each mental model object must include:\n  - `id` (kebab-case, unique)\n  - `title` (format: \"Cursor as a …\")\n  - `shortDescription` (1–2 sentences)\n  - `detailedExplanation` (array of 5 bullet strings)\n  - `relatedFeatures` (array of 4–6 strings, official Cursor feature names)\n  - `docs` (array of 1–3 objects with `label` and `url`)\n\n## Working with Mental Models\n\n### Adding New Mental Models\n- Use the command: `.cursor/commands/add-mental-model.md` for detailed instructions\n- Always validate terminology using Context7 MCP for official Cursor feature names\n- Prefer `docs.cursor.com` links when available\n- Ensure `id` values remain unique\n- Append new entries to the end of the JSON array\n\n### Modifying Existing Mental Models\n- Maintain the exact JSON schema\n- Keep formatting consistent with existing entries\n- Verify JSON validity (no trailing commas, correct quotes)\n- Test that the site still works after changes\n\n## Architecture Details\n\n### Data Flow\n```\nmental-models.json → app.js (loadData) → renderCards() → DOM\n```\n\n### Key Functions in app.js\n- `loadData()`: Fetches and parses JSON using `fetch()` API\n- `renderCards(models)`: Generates card HTML from data array\n- `renderModal(model)`: Generates modal content from selected model\n- `handleSearch()`: Filters models array by title (case-insensitive)\n- `openModal(model)`: Shows modal with model details\n- `closeModal()`: Hides modal overlay\n\n### Interaction Flow\n1. **Page Load**: Fetch JSON → Render all cards\n2. **Search**: User types → Filter array by title → Re-render filtered cards\n3. **Card Click**: Open modal → Populate with model details → Show overlay\n4. **Modal Close**: Click backdrop or close button → Hide modal\n\n## Related Files and Rules\n\n- **`.cursor/rules/clean-code.mdc`**: Guidelines for clean, maintainable code\n- **`.cursor/BUGBOT.md`**: Automated bug detection rules (TODO/FIXME, dangerous code patterns)\n- **`.cursor/commands/add-mental-model.md`**: Step-by-step guide for adding mental models\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n1. **Always validate Cursor terminology** using Context7 MCP before adding features or docs\n2. **Keep changes minimal** - This is a demo project, avoid over-engineering\n3. **Test locally** after any changes to ensure the site still works\n4. **Follow the JSON schema exactly** - Don't modify the structure without good reason\n5. **Use official Cursor documentation** - Prefer `docs.cursor.com` URLs\n6. **Maintain consistency** - Match existing code style and formatting\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Adding a Mental Model\n1. Read `.cursor/commands/add-mental-model.md` for detailed steps\n2. Use Context7 to verify official Cursor feature names\n3. Add exactly one new object to `data/mental-models.json`\n4. Test that the card appears and modal works\n\n### Fixing Bugs\n- Check `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` for automated bug detection rules\n- Follow the clean code guidelines in `.cursor/rules/clean-code.mdc`\n- Ensure JSON validity and test the site after fixes\n\n### Modifying UI/UX\n- Update `styles.css` for styling changes\n- Modify `app.js` for behavior changes\n- Keep the design simple and consistent with existing patterns\n- Test across different screen sizes (responsive grid layout)\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.2.36","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
