[2025-12-28 22:03:38] {"conversation_id":"09777441-707c-4cf9-aa51-601bbed9b11d","generation_id":"c0a62ede-9bf6-4b3d-8c0d-0c0d1d5f31da","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"get-library-docs","tool_input":"{\"context7CompatibleLibraryID\": \"/getcursor/docs\", \"mode\": \"code\", \"topic\": \"features\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"### Project-Specific AI Rules\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/rules-for-ai.mdx\\n\\nCreate a `.cursorrules` file in your project's root directory to define custom instructions for AI features. These instructions are specific to the project and are used by features like Cursor Chat and Ctrl/⌘ K.\\n\\n```text\\n.cursorrules\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Partial Accepts for Suggestions\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/advanced-features.mdx\\n\\nAccept parts of a suggestion, such as the next word, using a keybinding like `Ctrl/⌘` + Right Arrow. This feature requires enabling 'Cursor Tab' in Cursor Settings and allows for more granular control over accepting code suggestions.\\n\\n```editor\\nTo enable partial accepts:\\n1. Navigate to Cursor Settings.\\n2. Go to Features > Cursor Tab.\\n3. Set your preferred keybinding for `editor.action.inlineSuggest.acceptNextWord`.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Custom Review Instructions Example\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nProvides an example of custom instructions for the AI Review feature to focus on specific aspects of the code, such as performance.\\n\\n```plaintext\\nfocus on the performance of my code\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Long Context Chat Toggle\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/overview.mdx\\n\\nThis snippet explains how to enable and toggle different modes for the Long Context Chat feature, which allows for larger context windows.\\n\\n```markdown\\nYou can enable long context chat by going to `Cursor Settings` > `Beta` > `Long Context Chat`. With this enabled, you can toggle different chat modes through `Ctrl/⌘ .`.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### AI Fix Shortcut\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/overview.mdx\\n\\nThis snippet details the keyboard shortcut for triggering the AI fix feature, which helps resolve linter errors in the codebase.\\n\\n```markdown\\nTo do this, hover over the error in the editor, and click the blue AI fix button that shows up.\\n\\nThe keyboard shortcut for this would be to do `Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + E`.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Prediction for Edit Flow\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/advanced-features.mdx\\n\\nCursor can predict the next location you'll navigate to after accepting an edit. If prediction is available, pressing Tab allows you to move through subsequent edits sequentially, streamlining the editing process.\\n\\n```cpp\\nCursor predicts the next location for an edit, allowing sequential navigation through edits using the Tab key.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Tab in Peek Views\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/advanced-features.mdx\\n\\nUtilize Cursor's Tab functionality within 'Go to Definition' or 'Go to Type Definition' peek views. This is particularly helpful for tasks like adding new arguments to function calls and efficiently updating usages, especially when combined with Vim's `gd` command.\\n\\n```vim\\nIn vim, use `gd` to navigate to a function definition, modify it, and then use Cursor Tab in peek views to fix all usages in one go.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Example .cursorignore File\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/ignore-files.mdx\\n\\nThis snippet demonstrates how to configure a `.cursorignore` file to exclude directories, specific file types, and individual files from Cursor's features. It follows the same syntax as `.gitignore`.\\n\\n```plaintext\\n# Ignore all files in the `dist` directory\\ndist/\\n\\n# Ignore all `.log` files\\n*.log\\n\\n# Ignore specific file `config.json`\\nconfig.json\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Apply Code Block\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/apply.mdx\\n\\nIntegrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file. This feature allows for quick incorporation of AI-generated code, with changes visible in a diff view.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nApply Code Block:\\n  Description: Integrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file.\\n  Action: Click the play button in the top right corner of a chat code block.\\n  Result: Edits the file to incorporate the AI-generated code.\\n  Recommendation: Use for complex AI-driven code changes due to context and back-and-forth capabilities in Chat.\\n\\nAccept/Reject Changes:\\n  Description: Allows users to review and confirm or discard applied code changes.\\n  Accept Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Enter\\n  Reject Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Backspace\\n  UI Options: 'Accept' or 'Reject' buttons in the top right corner of the chat code block.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Review Options\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nLists the available options for initiating an AI Review, specifying which set of code changes to analyze.\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Working State\\n# This will review your uncommitted changes.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Diff with Main Branch\\n# This will review the diff between your current working state and the main branch.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Last Commit\\n# This will review the last commit you made.\\n```\"}]}","duration":736,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.2.36","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
