[2025-12-28 22:03:41] {"conversation_id":"09777441-707c-4cf9-aa51-601bbed9b11d","generation_id":"c0a62ede-9bf6-4b3d-8c0d-0c0d1d5f31da","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"get-library-docs","tool_input":"{\"context7CompatibleLibraryID\": \"/getcursor/docs\", \"mode\": \"code\", \"topic\": \"refactor\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"### Apply Code Block\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/apply.mdx\\n\\nIntegrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file. This feature allows for quick incorporation of AI-generated code, with changes visible in a diff view.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nApply Code Block:\\n  Description: Integrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file.\\n  Action: Click the play button in the top right corner of a chat code block.\\n  Result: Edits the file to incorporate the AI-generated code.\\n  Recommendation: Use for complex AI-driven code changes due to context and back-and-forth capabilities in Chat.\\n\\nAccept/Reject Changes:\\n  Description: Allows users to review and confirm or discard applied code changes.\\n  Accept Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Enter\\n  Reject Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Backspace\\n  UI Options: 'Accept' or 'Reject' buttons in the top right corner of the chat code block.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Re-install Mintlify Dependencies\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/README.md\\n\\nRe-installs Mintlify dependencies. Use this command if the `mintlify dev` command is not running correctly.\\n\\n```bash\\nmintlify install\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Changing Activity Bar Orientation\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/get-started/migrate-from-vscode.mdx\\n\\nExplains how to change the Activity Bar orientation in Cursor to the traditional vertical layout by modifying VS Code settings.\\n\\n```plaintext\\nOpen VS Code settings.\\nSet \\\"workbench.activityBar.orientation\\\" to \\\"vertical\\\".\\nRestart Cursor.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Install Mintlify CLI\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/README.md\\n\\nInstalls the Mintlify CLI globally, which is required for local development and previewing documentation changes.\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm i -g mintlify\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Review Options\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nLists the available options for initiating an AI Review, specifying which set of code changes to analyze.\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Working State\\n# This will review your uncommitted changes.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Diff with Main Branch\\n# This will review the diff between your current working state and the main branch.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Last Commit\\n# This will review the last commit you made.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Tab Functionality\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/overview.mdx\\n\\nDetails the capabilities of Cursor Tab, including its ability to suggest edits around the cursor, modify multiple lines, and base suggestions on recent changes and linter errors. It also specifies the range of lines it can modify.\\n\\n```cpp\\n// Cursor Tab can suggest edits around your cursor.\\n// It can modify multiple lines at once.\\n// Suggestions are based on recent changes and linter errors.\\n// Cursor can make changes from one line above to two lines below the current line.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Project-Specific AI Rules\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/rules-for-ai.mdx\\n\\nCreate a `.cursorrules` file in your project's root directory to define custom instructions for AI features. These instructions are specific to the project and are used by features like Cursor Chat and Ctrl/⌘ K.\\n\\n```text\\n.cursorrules\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Custom Review Instructions Example\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nProvides an example of custom instructions for the AI Review feature to focus on specific aspects of the code, such as performance.\\n\\n```plaintext\\nfocus on the performance of my code\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Start Local Development Server\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/README.md\\n\\nStarts the Mintlify development server to preview documentation changes locally. Ensure you are in the root directory containing mint.json.\\n\\n```bash\\nmintlify dev\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Prediction for Edit Flow\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/advanced-features.mdx\\n\\nCursor can predict the next location you'll navigate to after accepting an edit. If prediction is available, pressing Tab allows you to move through subsequent edits sequentially, streamlining the editing process.\\n\\n```cpp\\nCursor predicts the next location for an edit, allowing sequential navigation through edits using the Tab key.\\n```\"}]}","duration":566,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.2.36","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
